US-149 implemented and reported (`done-for-review`).

**What landed** (all in `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-links`, no `twenty-front` source touched):
- App-owned **Related** front-component panel, one entry per consumer target via a factory (sandbox renders empty props), listing outbound junction rows + inbound backlinks read from the persisted inverse relation `outgoingLinks`/`incomingLinks` — no read-time scan.
- Unreadable endpoints (server resolves the relation to `null`) are dropped; a failed junction query degrades to an empty panel (uninstall-safe).
- Empty state offers a "Lier…" action. Because a sandboxed front component cannot reach the host `SingleRecordPicker`, it searches the declared linkable set and writes the identical `a2eLink` row (same `linkKey`, same morph FKs), so both entry points share one store.
- Two app-owned standalone page-layout tabs: `document` (A2E Documents' layout) and standard `task` — so they vanish on uninstall (C3).
- Version bumped 0.1.1 → 0.1.2; README updated.

